\description{
These functions offer tools for projecting manynet-consistent data:
\itemize{
\item \code{to_mode()} projects a two-mode network to a one-mode network
of the node set given by the \code{mode} argument, which accepts either the
index of the mode or its name.
\item \code{to_mode1()} projects a two-mode network to a one-mode network
of the first node set's (e.g. rows) joint affiliations to nodes in the second node set (columns).
\item \code{to_mode2()} projects a two-mode network to a one-mode network
of the second node set's (e.g. columns) joint affiliations to nodes in the first node set (rows).
\item \code{to_linegraph()} projects a network to its line graph,
where the ties become nodes and incident nodes become their ties.
\item \code{to_hypergraph()} reformats one-mode or two-mode network data as hypergraph data,
where ties can connect more than two nodes.
\item \code{to_simplicial()} projects network data into a simplicial complex,
such as the maximal cliques of a one-mode network.
}
}
